  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A reduction in oil supply flow (production, exports, or transit throughput) directly raises the likelihood and potential magnitude of energy-supply interruptions by shrinking available physical and market buffers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_regional_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
