  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher perceived escalation risk induces state and proxy commanders to launch more preemptive, deterrent, or retaliatory strikes, raising the rate of offensive attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
