<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" target="europe_hybrid_threats::energy_supply_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.95</data>
  <data key="d37">War-related damage to infrastructure, deliberate export curbs and route disruptions reduce reliability of cross-border gas/LNG and electricity flows, directly degrading European energy supply stability.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" target="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A deterioration in energy supply stability (damaged infrastructure, export curbs or transit closures) directly increases the likelihood and potential magnitude of interruptions at global energy chokepoints such as pipelines, terminals and shipping routes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::investor_sentiment_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">War-related disruptions to energy supplies and higher electricity prices raise operating and capital costs for semiconductors and data centers, worsening investor sentiment toward capital-intensive segments of the U.S.-China tech competition.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" target="us_iran_regional_war::oil_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in energy supply stability from the Russia–Ukraine war (e.g., curtailed Russian exports or pipeline outages) directly reduces available global crude volumes and export throughput, tightening oil supply flows in markets tied to the US–Iran theatre within months.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_regional_war</data>
</edge>
