<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::attack_frequency" target="europe_hybrid_threats::cyber_intrusion_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in physical strikes against energy infrastructure prompts actors to conduct parallel cyber operations (to degrade command-and-control, disable backups, or create confusion), increasing unauthorized intrusions against European targets as part of coordinated hybrid campaigns.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::attack_frequency" target="russia_ukraine_war::intelligence_sharing" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in strikes against chokepoints creates immediate operational demand for coordinated maritime and energy-defense information, prompting faster and more complete bilateral and multilateral intelligence exchanges to protect shipping and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::attack_frequency" target="us_iran_regional_war::shipping_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in strikes and attacks in and around maritime chokepoints directly forces ship operators to suspend transits, reroute, seek naval escort, or cancel port calls, producing immediate route interruptions and delays.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
