<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" target="europe_hybrid_threats::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened risk of interrupted production or transport through a major energy chokepoint forces rerouting of shipping, port congestion, fuel shortages for logistics and emergency restrictions, producing more frequent and persistent commercial supply-chain interruptions in Europe.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">An increased likelihood of disruptions at global energy chokepoints directly reduces the continuity and predictability of fuel deliveries to the theater by forcing rerouting, canceling shipments, and triggering market/contractual interruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute increases in the risk of energy supply interruptions from a chokepoint prompt accelerated naval deployments, sanctions threats, and diplomatic pressure among consumers and suppliers—heightening interstate strategic friction between the U.S. and China over access and influence.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::media_attention" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising likelihood of energy cutoffs at a major chokepoint generates immediate news and social-media coverage linking supply-chain vulnerability to tech-sector risks, increasing attention on the US–China technology rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_chokepoint::energy_supply_risk" target="us_iran_regional_war::public_restraint" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising risk of supply interruptions prompts governments and major companies to issue public calls for de‑escalation and restraint to protect access to energy and stabilize markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_regional_war</data>
</edge>
