<edge source="europe_hybrid_threats::cyber_intrusion_rate" target="global_energy_chokepoint::defense_effectiveness" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher tempo of successful cyber intrusions degrades command-and-control, sensor feeds and intercept coordination for air/missile defenses, lowering detection and interception performance.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_chokepoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_hybrid_threats::cyber_intrusion_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::cyber_intrusion_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An uptick in unauthorized cyber operations in the European operational area reflects heightened attacker tempo and tooling that spill over into increased frequency and severity of intrusions against Ukrainian networks (shared targets, infrastructure, or mirrored campaigns).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_hybrid_threats::cyber_intrusion_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::info_security_vuln" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising tempo of cyber intrusions against European targets uncovers and exfiltrates credentials, tools and zero‑day knowledge used by multinational tech firms that operate in the US–China technology space, directly increasing measured information‑security vulnerabilities for actors in that rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="europe_hybrid_threats::cyber_intrusion_rate" target="us_iran_regional_war::escalation_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rising tempo of cyber intrusions in Europe attributed to Iranian state or proxy actors prompts U.S. military and intelligence warnings and risks misattribution or defensive/retaliatory moves, increasing perceived escalation risk in the US–Iran confrontation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">europe_hybrid_threats</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_regional_war</data>
</edge>
